1. Create a dataset with a TimestampType partition column containing an Instant with sub-second precision.
2. Write the dataset partitioned by that timestamp column to Parquet.
3. Read the Parquet data back and print the inferred schema.

Example code:
SparkSession spark = SparkSession.builder()
    .master("local[*]")
    .config("spark.sql.datetime.java8API.enabled", true)
    .config("spark.sql.session.timeZone", "UTC")
    .getOrCreate();

var inst = Instant.now();
StructType schema = new StructType(new StructField[]{
    DataTypes.createStructField("datacol", DataTypes.StringType, false),
    DataTypes.createStructField("partitioncol", DataTypes.TimestampType, false)
});
List<Row> data = List.of(RowFactory.create("test", inst));
Dataset<Row> ds = spark.createDataFrame(data, schema);
ds.write().mode(SaveMode.Overwrite).partitionBy("partitioncol").parquet("testdata");
spark.read().parquet("testdata").printSchema();

